{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417182-scion-2nd-help-in-calculate-injury-condition","id":1417182,"title":"Scion 2nd-Help in calculate injury condition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-07T12:09:56-07:00","id":1417182,"title":"Scion 2nd-Help in calculate injury condition","content":"Hello guys!<br /> <br /> I plan dun a scion game on hero tier Next month.<br /> <br /> But i kinda got confused in how calculate injury conditions,if someone got hit by a knife their can only get injured ir maimed condition? If thats it whats the big advantage of have high stamina? (Besides gets more hits from non lethal damage)<br /> <br /> I dont know if i got the right idea, but it seems lethal damage always will ignore bruised health box, i got it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T12:15:22-07:00","id":1417183,"title":"","content":"The player chooses the severity of the injury condition, as long as they have an open one. So, if I have Stamina 2, I start with a Bruised, Injured, and Maimed condition available. Now, say the satyr I'm fighting pulls a knife and inflicts an injury condition on me. I choose if I want to fill the Bruised, Injured, or Maimed condition. I can choose for whatever reason I want. I could go for Maimed in the hopes of using that to fill our Momentum pool. I could choose Bruised because I want to stay effective in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T12:28:12-07:00","id":1417186,"title":"","content":"Oh o see, so even if a character got struck by a sacred blade, the player can assume a bruised injured, i got it right?<br /> When i readed on book about the lethal tag, i got the wrong impression it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T12:35:08-07:00","id":1417189,"title":"","content":"I wish they had used a different name for the -1 levels.<br /> <br /> Or phrased the Lethal tag as &quot;This weapon deals cutting or stabbing injuries, such as <i>Deep Cut</i> or <i>Stabbed</i>&quot; rather than saying 'This weapon does not inflict a <i>Bruised</i> Injury Condition'<br /> <br /> But yes, a -1 Lethal Injury would be something like 'Dramatic Head Cut' or 'Tis But A Scratch'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T12:39:02-07:00","id":14